<article class="env-lemma" id="0C67">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C67">Lemma <span data-tag="0C67">55.9.8</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0C61" data-tag="0C61">55.9.3</a> set $d = \gcd (m_1, \ldots , m_ n)$ and let $D = \sum (m_ i/d)C_ i$ as an effective Cartier divisor. Then $\mathcal{O}_ X(D)$ has order dividing $d$ in $\mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}\nolimits (X)$ and $\mathcal{C}_{D/X}$ an invertible $\mathcal{O}_ D$-module of order dividing $d$ in $\mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}\nolimits (D)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{O}_ X(D)^{\otimes d} = \mathcal{O}_ X(dD) = \mathcal{O}_ X(X_ k) = \mathcal{O}_ X  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by Lemma <a href="/tag/0C5Z" data-tag="0C5Z">55.9.1</a>. We conclude as $\mathcal{C}_{D/X}$ is the pullback of $\mathcal{O}_ X(-D)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>